# secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# data: never commit medical images or the report corpus
data/images/
data/reports/
data/*.csv
data/*.zip

# DELIBERATE EXCEPTION: data/demo_cache.json IS committed.
# Streamlit Community Cloud only ever sees the repo, so the precomputed demo
# cannot work unless its cache ships with it. What is in there: model outputs
# plus 40 downscaled thumbnails from the Indiana University collection, which is
# public domain and de-identified with no data use agreement. No report text.
# The full corpus and full-resolution images stay out, as above.

# generated
artifacts/
traces/

# Raw eval records embed radiologist report text pulled from the corpus, and the
# corpus itself is gitignored. Committing them would smuggle the data back in by
# another route. The committed evidence is the summary, which carries the numbers
# without the patient text.
evals/results/
evals/ground_truth.json
evals/spot_checks/

# evals/gold_set.jsonl WAS ignored here. That was wrong and CI caught it.
#
# The reasoning was consistency: it embeds verbatim report sentences, and the
# corpus is ignored. But regenerating it needs the images AND the models, so a
# fresh clone cannot rebuild it -- which meant five tests that validate real
# gold-set properties (every named-case question forbids fuzzy search, the
# absence cases use regexes rather than brittle substrings) could not run in CI
# at all. Symbolic consistency was costing real coverage.
#
# What actually ships: ~8 single sentences from a public-domain, de-identified
# collection with no data use agreement. The full corpus stays out.
*.jsonl.gz
.cache/
